92186252296 1100 "It takes $4$ hours for a marathon runner to run $20$ miles at a constant pace. How long does it take for the marathon runner to run $26$ miles?" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252296 1113 #uuid "164076ec-371c-50b4-a03b-6cac29c4e58c" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252296 1145 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in miles per hour, we divide the number of miles, which is $20,$ by the number of hours, $4.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{4} & =20÷4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the marathon runner is $5$ miles per hour. \n\nTo find the time it takes the marathon runner to cover $26$ miles, we divide the distance by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{5} \\\\  & =26÷5 \\\\  & =5.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the marathon runner $5.2$ hours to run $26$ miles." 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252298 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252299 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252300 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252301 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252302 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1041 "selection" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252300 13194139533802 true] [17592186252297 1110 #uuid "dddb4291-2711-5f8f-92a9-a2985555457b" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252298 1034 "$4.8$ hours" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533802 true] [17592186252298 1111 #uuid "97fafd56-83f5-5cd1-8fdf-fa3e31d7d16c" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252299 1034 "$5.5$ hours" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252299 1103 #edb/ref 1759218