 $315$ meters at a constant pace. How long does it take for the dolphin to swim $396$ meters?" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252310 1113 #uuid "8c2b668e-96ec-5fdd-9ec2-92572bbaab20" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252310 1145 "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in meters per second, we divide the number of meters, which is $315,$ by the number of seconds, $35.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{315}{35} & =\\frac{315÷5}{35÷5} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{7} \\\\  & =63÷7 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the dolphin is $9$ meters per second. \n\nTo find the time it takes the dolphin to cover $396$ meters, we divide the distance by $9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{396}{9} \\\\  & =396÷9 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the dolphin $44$ seconds to travel $396$ meters." 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252312 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252313 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252314 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252315 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1000 #edb/ref 17592186252316 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1041 "selection" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1104 #edb/ref 17592186252312 13194139533802 true] [17592186252311 1110 #uuid "5a103802-ecc1-5fbd-99a2-e272206120e7" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252312 1034 "$44$ seconds" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533802 true] [17592186252312 1111 #uuid "2bd6fee4-993b-5272-84b2-bef9db3d4abe" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252313 1034 "$40$ seconds" 13194139533802 true] [17592186252313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139